It occurred to me the other day that though there are plenty of
monsters in Nethack with gaze attacks (Medusa, pyrolisk, floating eye,
Umber Hulk) there appears to be nothing with a *voice* attack. Yet
mythology is full of creatures that are able to use their voices
against people, to enchant them, drive them mad, or even kill them.

How about a new type of monster: the Lorelei (or Siren)? The Lorelei
would be a mermaid-type creature (always female) that lives in pools
of water or lakes. Although she is a very wimpy fighter, she is able
to lure you into the water using her voice. If you are within hearing
range (about 10 squares or so), and she successfully uses her voice
attack, you find yourself walking towards the water, one square per
turn. Any attempt to move away will instead cause you to move another
square towards the water; any attempt at a teleport spell will instead
automatically teleport you to the square next to the Lorelei (that is,
right into the water). Eventually, if you are unable to break the
spell or kill the Lorelei in time, you fall into the water (unless
wearing a ring of levitation or boots of water walking). There is a
certain chance (dependent on your intelligence, perhaps) that this
shocks you back to your senses, breaking the spell, and you clamber
out of the water in the usual way. Otherwise, you drown (unless
wearing "oMB, of course.) The Lorelei's spell can be prevented or
nullified by wearing a ring of free action, wearing earplugs (new
item), or lighting a candle and then (W)earing it to plug your ears
with wax (this idea is taken from Greek mythology). I suppose it could
also be countered by a musical attack of your own, such as a harp of
taming or a horn of scare monster. If a Lorelei was on the level, you
would get periodic warnings as with a mind flayer: "You hear a
beautiful voice raised in distant song."

What do you think? Any other ideas for monsters with voice attacks?

